{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/821182-crossed-wings-denial-what-does-this-do","id":821182,"title":"Crossed Wings Denial: what does this do?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-01T13:42:34-08:00","id":821182,"title":"Crossed Wings Denial: what does this do?","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">For the record:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#9F0B10\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>&quot;Cost: </b><span style=\"color:#000000\">6m, 4i<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Type: </b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Reflexive</span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">The perfection of the martial artist\u2019s defense is like the <span style=\"color:#000000\">beauty of the crane, so absolute in its calm refinement that <span style=\"color:#000000\">seemingly nothing could ever disturb it. The martial artist <span style=\"color:#000000\">makes a (Wits + Martial Arts) roll that cannot be enhanced <span style=\"color:#000000\">by magic, and banks all successes. Until her next turn, she <span style=\"color:#000000\">may spend successes to add to her Parry on a one-for-one <span style=\"color:#000000\">basis. Alternatively, she may expend a success after <span style=\"color:#000000\">successfully blocking an attack to respond with a <span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>decisive</b> <span style=\"color:#000000\">counterattack</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Why would I use this? Ever? <span style=\"color:#000000\">I have no idea how this Charm even works. Are you spending the successes before the attack roll, making this 6m 4i for <i>maybe</i> +5 total Defense? That might be the worst Excellency in Exalted history - well, except for the Terrestrial version of the same Charm, where you'd be luck to get +3 Defense for that same investment. Do you apply them after the attack, or as a non-Charm bonus, despite nothing in the official wording indicating that? Why are you paying 4i to get a resource which can be cashed in for Counterattacks if you could just take Full Defense for no Motes and fewer Initiative to get a non-Charm Defense bonus and unlimited Counterattacks with your Form Charm?<br /> <br /> I don't know. I am baffled. I've become reasonably proficient in 3E rules, but I need help making some sense of what this is trying to accomplish.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T14:28:40-08:00","id":821213,"title":"","content":"CWD is Reflexive, so if you need to make another action, it's better than full defense? Or you use both of them together, so that ~5 times, you can respond to an attack with Crane Form's withering counterattack and then follow that up with CWD's decisive counterattack? (both these Charm lack the Counterattack keyword, so this interpretation is super-RAW, although its RAI is questionable)<br /> <br /> That's all I got off the top of my head.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5454-mcallister","name":"McAllister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5454_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T14:57:12-08:00","id":821224,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>McAllister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/821182-crossed-wings-denial-what-does-this-do?p=821213#post821213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">CWD is Reflexive, so if you need to make another action, it's better than full defense? Or you use both of them together, so that ~5 times, <b>you can respond to an attack with Crane Form's withering counterattack and then follow that up with CWD's decisive counterattack?</b> (both these Charm lack the Counterattack keyword, so this interpretation is super-RAW, although its RAI is questionable)</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">IIRC Crane Style offers the only withering counterattack in the book.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">It is also, iirc, the only combat ability other than Melee or Brawl to offer counterattacks, period. The \u201cboost your Parry\u201d button is there as an option, but really the point of this is to jump in front of an ally, take the attack, and counterattack ad infinitum. In fact, I don't read the Charm as limiting you to just one counterattack per turn from CWD either.</span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/K9a6Pmp.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/998-korhal_iv","name":"Korhal_IV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"592"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T15:56:18-08:00","id":821270,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the thoughts, folks.<br /> <br /> Hurm. The more I look at Crane Style's counterattack tech, the more it bugs me. It is <i>so</i> much more vague than the Melee/Brawl equivalents. An innate Over-And-Under Method interaction between those two Charms does make Crossed Wings suddenly worthwhile, but is that how it works? Do the Counterattacks resolve before or after the triggers? Since they don't have the Keyword, can someone else technically Counterattack back at them? And why exactly isn't Humbling Enlightenment Commentary a Gambit.<br /> <br /> Ugh. I thought we were done with unclearly-written Martial Arts which interface questionably with the actual rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T16:21:31-08:00","id":821287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/821182-crossed-wings-denial-what-does-this-do?p=821270#post821270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ugh. I thought we were done with unclearly-written Martial Arts which interface questionably with the actual rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems to me that the vagueness derives from the MA chapter assuming that there would be some kind of general counterattack mechanics that would be included in an earlier chapter (say, the systems chapter), and basically just referenced them versus spelling out the rules in the MA chapter all over again. But there wound up being no such rules in the system chapter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T17:23:18-08:00","id":821319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/821182-crossed-wings-denial-what-does-this-do?p=821287#post821287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems to me that the vagueness derives from the MA chapter assuming that there would be some kind of general counterattack mechanics that would be included in an earlier chapter (say, the systems chapter), and basically just referenced them versus spelling out the rules in the MA chapter all over again. But there wound up being no such rules in the system chapter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Almost certainly! And there's probably similar reasons for the wonkiness of Humbling Enlightenment Commentary (which might predate both Gambits and the notion that you could just take normal Social Influence actions in combat time), the general lack of definition in Mournful Crane's Cry (which can both fling someone two Range Bands without even having to do damage <i>and</i> create a duplicate Death Ray), and Wisdom of the Celestial Crane's missing Psyche Keyword.<br /> <br /> That's the Malfeas of it: I know the current team know the system, since they made it. And I know they care, since this whole edition is an insane labor of passion. But somehow, this never-fixed prototype still snuck into the Backer PDF, hitting EX3 faster even than Scroll of the Monk hit EX2. That's regrettable - I guess when I finish my current project, I'll have to go back and take a stab at updating it. Sadly, this will look like a massive nerf to anyone using the Style as it's currently written.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T17:30:16-08:00","id":821324,"title":"","content":"There are some other mechanics issues in the backer PDF - see the Craft or Lore Charms that interact with the old Evocation paradigm. So it's not just with Crane. I only hope the Crane stuff made it into the errata report.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T17:55:45-08:00","id":821337,"title":"","content":"My guess is that the purpose of the charm is to allow crane stylists who use another form to have access to counterattacks when using that form's style.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10317-skina-stonedottir","name":"Skina Stonedottir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10317_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T18:02:36-08:00","id":821339,"title":"","content":"CWD can be used when you're not in Crane Form, so that's a plus. If you're using another MA's form or just haven't had a good moment to get into Crane's, this gives you an easy counterattack. Also, Crane Form may function more as a deterrent that eats your actions, depending on how the ST handles system transparency wrt NPCs, whereas CWD lets you be aggressive and still retaliate. With only Crane Form an opponent may choose to go after allies you're not protecting or accomplish other objectives; with CWD you can still force a confrontation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"color:#696969\">When all the world was very young<br /> And mountain magic heavy hung<br /> The supermen would walk in file<br /> Guardians of a loveless isle</span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2010-root","name":"Root","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1014"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T19:23:35-08:00","id":821373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/821182-crossed-wings-denial-what-does-this-do?p=821270#post821270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Hurm. The more I look at Crane Style's counterattack tech, the more it bugs me. It is <i>so</i> much more vague than the Melee/Brawl equivalents. An innate Over-And-Under Method interaction between those two Charms does make Crossed Wings suddenly worthwhile, but is that how it works?</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">It's a withering attack, followed by a decisive attack. So not precisely Over-and-Under Method, but analogous.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/821182-crossed-wings-denial-what-does-this-do?p=821270#post821270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do the Counterattacks resolve before or after the triggers?</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Generally, a counterattack lands before the attack that caused it, ne?</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/821182-crossed-wings-denial-what-does-this-do?p=821270#post821270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since they don't have the Keyword, can someone else technically Counterattack back at them?</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Correct. The point of keywords is to not have to reiterate simple rules like that every time. The omission of a keyword can be a bonus or a penalty that way.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/821182-crossed-wings-denial-what-does-this-do?p=821270#post821270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And why exactly isn't Humbling Enlightenment Commentary a Gambit.</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Because it lets you make an instill action with your (Dex+MA) pool, which is generally not what gambits do. Gambits let you unhorse, disarm, grapple, distract \u2013 they're combat maneuvers, not social influence actions. Also because it sets up Kindly Sifu's Quill to inflict a penalty.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/821182-crossed-wings-denial-what-does-this-do?p=821319#post821319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the general lack of definition in Mournful Crane's Cry (which can both fling someone two Range Bands without even having to do damage <i>and</i> create a duplicate Death Ray)</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Flinging someone two range bands without dealing damage is a nerf, not a bonus. It means you are still dealing with an angry enemy closing the distance, not a dead enemy.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">The duplicate Death Ray part you'll have to explain to me. Honestly, these last three complaints read like you're actively searching for problems.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/821182-crossed-wings-denial-what-does-this-do?p=821319#post821319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and Wisdom of the Celestial Crane's missing Psyche Keyword.</div> </div> </div> </div>No Charm described as inspiring emotion through extraordinary skill has the Psyche keyword (Infectious Zealotry Approach, Monk-Seducing Demon Dance, and Celestial Bliss Trick, among others).</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Only Charms that bypass the social influence system entirely - like Memory-Reweaving Discipline, Mind-Swallowing Missive, and Hypnotic Tongue Technique, get the Psyche keyword.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Wisdom of the Celestial Crane inflicts a Tie, but it doesn't bypass the social influence system (for example, an Abyssal hit with a Defining Tie to Creation might still feel that the people living in it would suffer less if they were ghosts...) So it falls closer to Celestial Bliss Trick than to Hypnotic Tongue Technique.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">That said, as someone who plays a Crane stylist, if you wanted to add the Psyche keyword to Wisdom of the Celestial Crane, I wouldn't object strenuously. It's a comparatively small nerf, and WotCC's effects could be read one way or another depending on how much you emphasize the \u201csacred beauty\u201d of the Celestial Crane vis-a-vis the effects of having one's head hammered repeatedly by graceful kicks.</span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/K9a6Pmp.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/998-korhal_iv","name":"Korhal_IV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"592"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T19:23:59-08:00","id":821374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/821182-crossed-wings-denial-what-does-this-do#post821182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would I use this? Ever?<br /> ...<br /> Why are you paying 4i to get a resource which can be cashed in for Counterattacks if you could just take Full Defense for no Motes and fewer Initiative to get a non-Charm Defense bonus and unlimited Counterattacks with your Form Charm?</div> </div> </div> </div>Suppose you are walking along one day when a very vicious youth throws a rock or two thousand at you. No problem, you say. &quot;I'll just block them and reflect them back at him with Feather-Stirred Arrow Deflection.&quot; A good plan, except you are neither in Crane Form nor have taken a full defense action. You block the first rock or twenty-two, but you soon tire, falter and die.<br /> <br /> But if you had Crossed Wings Denial, you could have counterattacked anyway. With Wisdom of the Celestial Crane you could have both knocked him out in one blow and befriended him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10881-anasurimbor","name":"Anasurimbor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T04:58:07-08:00","id":821549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korhal_IV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/821182-crossed-wings-denial-what-does-this-do?p=821373#post821373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[COLOR=#252c2f]<span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Generally, a counterattack lands before the attack that caused it, ne?</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Ne.<br /> <br /> There is no &quot;generally&quot;. There is no general case laid out anywhere. Like multiattacks, the actual rules of every Counterattack Charm are spelled out in the Charm which creates them, and they all work differently. The only place &quot;Counterattack&quot; appears outside of specific Charm descriptions is a Keyword - which, we have established, these Charms lack*. Since &quot;make Withering and Decisive Counterattacks&quot; is not a rules action the way that something like &quot;make Rush and Disengage actions&quot; would be, I could argue that that Charm does nothing, or that it lets you treat diseases, and technically have the same level of rules backing as saying that it lets you attack anyone who swings at you before their attack resolves.<br /> <br /> But obviously, that's a silly example. &quot;Counterattack&quot; may not be a rules term, but it is comprehensible English. Let's see if we can make a reasonable theory of authorial intent. Among the Solar combat charms, there are 5 Counterattack Charms**:<ul><li>Solar Cross-Counter (3m, 1i, 1wp): After taking Withering damage, make a Decisive attack with damage equal to the damage you just took, rather than your own Initiative.</li> <li>Solar Counterattack (3m): After being hit but before damage is rolled, make an otherwise-normal Decisive attack.</li> <li>Ready in Eight Directions Stance (5m): Until your next turn, respond to every attack which hits with a Solar Counter Attack - your Initiative does not reset until then.</li> <li>Flashing Edge of Dawn (4m 1wp): After being hit but before damage is rolled, make a Withering Attack. Instead of gaining the Initiative the target loses, roll it against them as Decisive damage.</li> <li>Over-And-Under Method (7m, 1wp): Make a Clash attack (Fervent Blow) and use Flashing Edge of Dawn against the same attack. Note that this will never let you actually hit the enemy twice: you'd have to lose the Clash to ever trigger the Counterattack.</li> </ul><br /> Note that <i>none</i> of these can &quot;land before the attack that caused it&quot;. Note that none of them can increase your Initiative, either. And that none of them will let you hit the same person out of turn more than once.<br /> <br /> So I'm glad that your group has found an interpretation of Crane Style that works in your game. However, I don't think that interpretation works across EX3 in general: the rules are vague and often confusing, and their most obvious interpretation - allowing scenelong Initiative-increasing Counterattacks which resolve before the attacks which trigger them, and can possibly happen 6-7 times off of a single trigger - is outrageously broken, letting Dragon-Bloods be vastly superior to native Solar Charms in their area of focus. I hope that someone quicker than I caught this during the errata period, or that the writers noticed it themselves, and it will be fixed.<br /> <br /> But until that time, I urge STs to strongly consider banning or seriously reworking the style. I like the core concept of Crane more than almost any other Martial Art, but its current execution is a mistake, and can cause serious problems.<br /> <br /> <br /> * Do not underestimate how big of a hole in the rules that omission is, either - it means that, for example, if you attack someone and they Clash you, you can <i>counterattack the Clash</i>. But that's a really easy fix compared to how dysfunctional the rest of Crane is.<br /> ** There are three more in other Abilities: Asp Bites Its Tail turns attempts to undercut you back on the person who took them, Effective Counterargument raises someone else's Resolve after an Influence action is rolled, and Rousing Backlash Assault has the same problems with assuming &quot;counterattack&quot; would be defined elsewhere in the book that Crane does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":2168,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","user":"Chejop Kejak","date":". 02-02-2016, 02:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T01:15:40-08:00","id":822192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>McAllister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/821182-crossed-wings-denial-what-does-this-do?p=821213#post821213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or you use both of them together, so that ~5 times, you can respond to an attack with Crane Form's withering counterattack and then follow that up with CWD's decisive counterattack? (both these Charm lack the Counterattack keyword, so this interpretation is super-RAW, although its RAI is questionable)</div> </div> </div> </div>The Counterattack keyword (or lack thereof) is largely irrelevant, as 3e generally uses keywords in a descriptive rather than prescriptive fashion. Adding the keyword to Crane Form and CWD would also create the possible issue that they couldn't be used to help parry a counterattack, and also that you couldn't reflexively enter Crane Form by blocking a decisive counterattack.<br /> <br /> The big problem is that we don't have hard rules for counterattacks. I suppose it's possible they can be used together, as they do trigger off separate events, but this interpretation would also allow stacking Solar Counterattack with Solar-Cross Counter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korhal_IV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/821182-crossed-wings-denial-what-does-this-do?p=821224#post821224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IIRC Crane Style offers the only withering counterattack in the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Black Claw also has a withering counterattack. Nightingale has the incredibly nasty Hearing the Heart Song, which let's you counterattack an evaded decisive attack via a read intentions action against their Guile. It gets (Evasion) non-charm dice and each extra success steals a point of initiative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10881-anasurimbor","name":"Anasurimbor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T02:20:46-08:00","id":822211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anasurimbor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/821182-crossed-wings-denial-what-does-this-do?p=822192#post822192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Black Claw also has a withering counterattack. Nightingale has the incredibly nasty Hearing the Heart Song, which let's you counterattack an evaded decisive attack via a read intentions action against their Guile. It gets (Evasion) non-charm dice and each extra success steals a point of initiative.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically, there's also Flashing Edge of Dawn/Over-And-Under Method, but as noted above, that can't increase your own Initiative the way something like HtHS does - you're not wrong, that Charm is sick. It also implies to me that the Martial Arts used a different philosophy of counterattacks than the finalized Solar Charmset, but at least it has a narrower trigger (Evading a Decisive attack), and costs Initiative to attempt, so there's some risk. Oh, and, it <i>actually has rules for how it works</i>.<br /> <br /> That's not how Crane rolls, basically ever.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T07:03:03-08:00","id":822347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anasurimbor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/821182-crossed-wings-denial-what-does-this-do?p=822192#post822192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Counterattack keyword (or lack thereof) is largely irrelevant, as 3e generally uses keywords in a descriptive rather than prescriptive fashion. Adding the keyword to Crane Form and CWD would also create the possible issue that they couldn't be used to help parry a counterattack, and also that you couldn't reflexively enter Crane Form by blocking a decisive counterattack.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I don't buy your first assertion for a second, if I understand what you mean by prescriptive. Keywords apply rules, period. If Crane Form and CWD both had the Counterattack keyword, you would be unable to use both of them in response to the same attack: they don't, so you can. The existence of the Counterattack keyword suggests to me that this might not be intended, but it's sure as hell RAW.<br /> <br /> Oh, are you referring to the fact that the majority of Charms that have keywords also explain what those keywords do? That's one of the most frustrating decisions I can imagine.<br /> <br /> As for the non-attack portions of the Charms failing to interact if they had the Counterattack keyword, you're right. I'd be delighted if, for the finished product, the devs 1. tightened up the wording of the keywords, 2. promised us very solemnly that they had been applied in every instance they had been intended to apply, and 3. stopped reiterating their effects in every Charm that has them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5454-mcallister","name":"McAllister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5454_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T09:15:35-08:00","id":822450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>McAllister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/821182-crossed-wings-denial-what-does-this-do?p=822347#post822347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I don't buy your first assertion for a second, if I understand what you mean by prescriptive. Keywords apply rules, period. <b>If Crane Form and CWD both had the Counterattack keyword, you would be unable to use both of them in response to the same attack: they don't, so you can</b>. The existence of the Counterattack keyword suggests to me that this might not be intended, but it's sure as hell RAW.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure that's true (although I agree with your assessment otherwise). If they had the Counterattack keyword, you could not use one of them to respond to a counterattack made by the other, but it's not clear to me that there's anything RAW that prevents activating multiple Counterattack-tagged effects in response to a single stimulus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T09:22:05-08:00","id":822452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/821182-crossed-wings-denial-what-does-this-do?p=822450#post822450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure that's true (although I agree with your assessment otherwise). If they had the Counterattack keyword, you could not use one of them to respond to a counterattack made by the other, but it's not clear to me that there's anything RAW that prevents activating multiple Counterattack-tagged effects in response to a single stimulus.</div> </div> </div> </div>:|<br /> <br /> You're right.<br /> <br /> I wish they would tell us that multiple counterattacks in response to one trigger was their intention, if it was.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5454-mcallister","name":"McAllister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5454_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T11:41:14-08:00","id":823554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>McAllister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/821182-crossed-wings-denial-what-does-this-do?p=822452#post822452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wish they would tell us that multiple counterattacks in response to one trigger was their intention, if it was.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually assume it was their intention, since that rule existed in 2E and is now conspicuous by its absence.<br /> <br /> I think it's a terrible intention, and should be houseruled into a crater. But I <i>think</i> that's at least a deliberate choice, and not a huge oversight. I really hope so.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T11:45:20-08:00","id":823562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/821182-crossed-wings-denial-what-does-this-do?p=823554#post823554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually assume it was their intention, since that rule existed in 2E and is now conspicuous by its absence.<br /> <br /> I think it's a terrible intention, and should be houseruled into a crater. But I <i>think</i> that's at least a deliberate choice, and not a huge oversight. I really hope so.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the perpetual 3e riddle, right? &quot;Throw away all your 2e preconceptions! Usually!&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm really hoping for a &quot;COUNTERATTACKS&quot; section in the combat rules, whenever the final release is. We'll see!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T15:01:39-07:00","id":876021,"title":"","content":"My interpretation:<br /> <br /> Neither Crane Form nor Cross Winged Denial have the counterattack keyword<br /> Neither have the stackable keyword<br /> CWD say &quot;may expend <b>a</b> success&quot; (emphasis added)<br /> <br /> Thus, RAW,<br /> <br /> You can respond to an attack with a withering counter from CF and <i>a single</i> decisive from CWD.<br /> <br /> (RAI might exclude attacks with the Clash or counterattack keywords.)<br /> <br /> Going by 2E timing, your counterattacks happen after the triggering attack is resolved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 04-28-2016, 04:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T15:11:16-07:00","id":876036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>McAllister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/821182-crossed-wings-denial-what-does-this-do?p=822452#post822452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wish they would tell us that multiple counterattacks in response to one trigger was their intention, if it was.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not, barring stuff that specifically says it can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T19:30:54-07:00","id":876199,"title":"","content":"A well-reasoned theory about how these Charms should work, followed immediately by a partial clarification (thanks!), which explains that the above theory is wrong. For my money, either interation is too good for Martial Arts - especially in the form where Dragon-Bloods can use them.<br /> <br /> I continue to urge everybody to ban or totally re-write this Style.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T01:27:28-07:00","id":876355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/821182-crossed-wings-denial-what-does-this-do?p=876036#post876036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not, barring stuff that specifically says it can.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then Crane Style is awful. Like, really, really awful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T02:11:51-07:00","id":876380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/821182-crossed-wings-denial-what-does-this-do?p=876355#post876355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then Crane Style is awful. Like, really, really awful.</div> </div> </div> </div>In what kind of bizzaro world is <i>only </i>getting one free withering or decisive attack every time anyone attacks you or any of your buddies really, really awful? And you get that from just two of its many charms, mind you. I don't understand how you could possibly reach this conclusion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T04:43:29-07:00","id":876477,"title":"","content":"The bizzaro bit is where you can't attack and lose 4i each round.<br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> Decisive counterattacking for your buddies (with CWD) is NINE motes a pop, and you're losing 4i, and you're rolling a random number of counter attacks AND you have to successfully Parry in order to counter.<br /> <br /> Resetting to base each time... That's one decisive counterattack against you or your buddies... Then you Crash yourself. Yay.<br /> <br /> If you're using Crane Form to counterattack, then you're giving up your action to gamble on what your opponent does. With Exalted's system transparency... this is not ideal. But if you are willing to use CF... Why would you ever use CWD? If you've got CF up, CDW is an Excellency that bleeds initiative AS WELL AS motes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 04-29-2016, 05:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T05:17:34-07:00","id":876500,"title":"","content":"The first three Charms alone make Crane an incredibly robust group defence/counterattack set. I have no idea what you guys are complaining about.<br /> <br /> Fluttering Cry of Warning seems pretty straightforward to me. It lets you make a Decisive counterattack against an enemy that attacks you. Unless you are in Full Defence, this doesn't meet the conditions to counterattack with Crane Form. <br /> <br /> If you are being attacked and you have a healthy initiative track, use FCoW in response. Add all but one of the rolled successes to your Parry. If the defence is successful, apply counterattack. If the attack is unlikely to meet your regular Parry you can always bank the successes and use them to defend against additional attacks during the turn, but this is secondary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":2093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","user":"Crumplepunch","date":". 04-28-2016, 08:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T05:28:50-07:00","id":876505,"title":"","content":"The charm is Cross Winged Denial, FCoW is something different.<br /> CDW has Crane Form as a prerequisite.<br /> The issue at hand was &quot;what if you DO meet the conditions to counterattack in Crane Form&quot;.<br /> How are you getting a healthy initiative track from taking Full Defence?<br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> Crane Form is useful because FCoW lets you defend your Circle. Even if opponents look at you and say &quot;nope&quot;, you still get to attack on behalf of your allies. At a mote cost.<br /> <br /> Cross Winged Denial was useful because after countering with a Withering from CF, you now had initiative to blow on the charm's activation cost (and Decisive damage).<br /> <br /> Either or means either CF or CWD is a speedbump.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 04-28-2016, 08:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T05:34:13-07:00","id":876509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/821182-crossed-wings-denial-what-does-this-do?p=876505#post876505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The charm is Cross Winged Denial, FCoW is something different.<br /> CDW has Crane Form as a prerequisite.<br /> The issue at hand was &quot;what if you DO meet the conditions to counterattack in Crane Form&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oops, yes, I did mean Crossed Wing Denial.<br /> <br /> So... what, you wanted a withering counterattack immediately followed by a decisive counterattack? That's nuts, man.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T05:46:10-07:00","id":876521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/821182-crossed-wings-denial-what-does-this-do?p=876509#post876509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oops, yes, I did mean Crossed Wing Denial.<br /> <br /> So... what, you wanted a withering counterattack immediately followed by a decisive counterattack? That's nuts, man.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Or a printed Melee charm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9124-satoshi","name":"satoshi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T07:14:22-07:00","id":876597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/821182-crossed-wings-denial-what-does-this-do?p=876509#post876509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oops, yes, I did mean Crossed Wing Denial.<br /> <br /> So... what, you wanted a withering counterattack immediately followed by a decisive counterattack? That's nuts, man.</div> </div> </div> </div>And not actually counter to the rules as printed.<br /> <br /> Like, we know it's incorrect, because it was illegal in 2e, which had rules for counterattacks, and one can assume that 3e inherits those rules. But there's nothing that restricts your use of multiple counterattack effects actually in the book; for someone coming to it cold, &quot;the great thing with Crane Style is I can stack all these counterattacks!&quot; is a perfectly reasonable conclusion.<br /> <br /> It can't be overstressed that the biggest problem with Crane isn't Crane; it's that Crane assumes, quite reasonably, that the book is going to have told you how counterattacks work, and the book <i>does not do that thing</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T09:45:51-07:00","id":876744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/821182-crossed-wings-denial-what-does-this-do?p=876597#post876597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It can't be overstressed that the biggest problem with Crane isn't Crane; it's that Crane assumes, quite reasonably, that the book is going to have told you how counterattacks work, and the book <i>does not do that thing</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. Absolutely.<br /> <br /> Crane Style is a sad case where the original design team managed to &quot;Scroll of the Monk&quot; themselves. The rigors of a long development cycle meant that the rules were in a different place at the end than when Crane was written, and it shows. It's broken in the truest sense - a piece of mechanics which, as written, <i>does not work</i>.<br /> <br /> (Also, I think that pre-emptive counterattacks which can net you Initiative are overpowered in any case - certainly, native Solar Charms can't do that. However, that's effectively a non-issue, because it's impossible to meaningfully say whether a Charm without rules is strong or weak.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T09:57:32-07:00","id":876752,"title":"","content":"This is silly.<br /> <br /> Vance (who wrote the style, I'm pretty sure) already said that you can't make more than one counterattack in response to an attack. Crane's counterattacks are made after the initiating attack is resolved.<br /> <br /> There, done, now you can stop bewailing this Scroll of the Monk redux disaster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T10:05:07-07:00","id":876760,"title":"","content":"Cool. Can I use them in response to Clashes/other Counterattacks? What dice pool do I use? Do they happen before or after the &quot;triggering attacks&quot; - or &quot;after the attack roll but before damage,&quot; like the Melee ones do?<br /> <br /> Those are ALL problems created by the vagueness in the Style <i>in addition to all the other problems with Counterattacks in 3rd</i>, such as whether your Crashing/killing someone stops their attack from resolving. Clearing up a single point does not suddenly make all these problems go away. I really appreciate Vance stepping in here, and I don't want to sound accusatory - with a long, complex project such as this, a few mistakes are inevitable, even if the lack of updates after the Back PDF is regrettable. But saying that this is all magically fixed forever by a single clarification is just not true.<br /> <br /> If people have interpretations that for their games, more power to them. But the Charms as written in the book don't have any clear meaning, and in my experience, that's a minefield in mechanically-deep combat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T10:11:24-07:00","id":876765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/821182-crossed-wings-denial-what-does-this-do?p=876760#post876760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/821182-crossed-wings-denial-what-does-this-do?p=876760#post876760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can I use them in response to Clashes/other Counterattacks?</div> </div> </div> </div>No.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/821182-crossed-wings-denial-what-does-this-do?p=876760#post876760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What dice pool do I use?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dex + MA, same as any other Crane attack.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/821182-crossed-wings-denial-what-does-this-do?p=876760#post876760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do they happen before or after the &quot;triggering attacks&quot; - or &quot;after the attack roll but before damage,&quot; like the Melee ones do?</div> </div> </div> </div>After the triggering attacks. This also resolves the problem of whether or not it disrupts the attack (it does not).<br /> <br /> Yes, there is the occasional ellision here and there, but filling in the blanks should not be a challenge for someone with your evident mechanical chops. I mean, I've been using Crane Style with one of my characters, and nobody at my table even noticed there were even any problems to solve, so evident were the solutions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T10:19:08-07:00","id":876771,"title":"","content":"As I said, that's fine, but you're making it up. It's not actual rules text. I can make things up just fine without you acting smugly superior, thanks.<br /> <br /> I have no way to know whether you're being deliberately obtuse, or if the idea that I would like rules to provide a framework to resolve things is just a lot more complicated than it seems to me. In either case, neither of us is likely to communicate anything new to the other at this point.<br /> <br /> I intend to keep an eye on this thread in case anything new does come up - I'll be trying not to rehash this debate, so as to avoid burying anything actually interesting which might get posted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T13:26:45-07:00","id":876916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/821182-crossed-wings-denial-what-does-this-do?p=876477#post876477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The bizzaro bit is where you can't attack and lose 4i each round.<br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> Decisive counterattacking for your buddies is NINE motes a pop, and you're losing 4i, and you're rolling a random number of counter attacks AND you have to successfully Parry in order to counter.<br /> <br /> Resetting to base each time... That's one decisive counterattack against you or your buddies... Then you Crash yourself. Yay.</div> </div> </div> </div>...Have you looked at the Form charm? Counterattacking is free, whether it's withering or decisive. Crossed Wings Denial is a cheap parry booster that also has a situational use of letting you throw out counterattacks when you don't have time to put the Form up or couldn't go full defence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T02:49:30-07:00","id":877494,"title":"","content":"It's six motes 4i. That's not cheap. I'd rather use the Excellency.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T04:46:05-07:00","id":877557,"title":"","content":"With maxed pools you get an average of 6 successes using it, which lets you get +6 parry. Using an excellency that would cost you 12m. It's not super-duper bargain basement discount cheap, but if you're running low on motes it's a very nice option to have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T12:38:54-07:00","id":1212752,"title":"","content":"(I realize this is much-belated, but having the last post in a thread about answering mechanical questions be factually wrong seemed like the greater evil.)<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/821182-crossed-wings-denial-what-does-this-do?p=877557#post877557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With maxed pools you get an average of 6 successes using it, which lets you get +6 parry. Using an excellency that would cost you 12m. It's not super-duper bargain basement discount cheap, but if you're running low on motes it's a very nice option to have.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be clear, it cannot do that. You can't use all 6 of the Parry bonus on your defense at once, unless you somehow have a dice cap that high. And Solar's don't. The only way I know of to make that work is by being an Essence 6+ Sidereal, at which point you could attain the same effect with Excellencies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T12:56:38-07:00","id":1212764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/821182-crossed-wings-denial-what-does-this-do?p=1212752#post1212752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(I realize this is much-belated, but having the last post in a thread about answering mechanical questions be factually wrong seemed like the greater evil.)<br /> <br /> To be clear, it cannot do that. You can't use all 6 of the Parry bonus on your defense at once, unless you somehow have a dice cap that high. And Solar's don't. The only way I know of to make that work is by being an Essence 6+ Sidereal, at which point you could attain the same effect with Excellencies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay? Not sure why you did a two year necro to be pedantic at a post that wasn't even incorrect. Yes, you can't throw all six points of parry-boosting at a single attack. Given that past me was saying &quot;hey, this gives you some improved mote economy&quot; and not &quot;hey, this lets you break your dice cap&quot;, I figured that people reading this thread would both know the base rules of the game and intuit that I was talking about blocking multiple attacks. If some new player came to a thread on the power level of a specific martial arts charm looking to find guidance on how much Solars are allowed to boost their parry then I apologise for any confusion caused.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}